# A PRUNED WORKTREE COMES BACK FROM THE DEAD. The recorded path is reused by an
# unrelated checkout and the run becomes `Verified` again — a dead run offered
# as an attach candidate into a working tree that has nothing to do with it.
contains: a path reused by an unrelated directory must not revive a dead run

# A NON-SESSION FILE BECOMES A RUN RECORD. `<root>/decoy.jsonl` is under the
# project root, so the pre-fix rule loads it into the catalog and the inventory
# answers with a run the session files never described. The same rule admits a
# `..` traversal, a nested path, a missing file, a symlink, and a record whose
# file identity has moved on.
contains: must not be admitted as a session record

# THE SEMANTIC CLAIM, REACHED ON ITS OWN. orgasmic:TASK-FZB6T.3 finding 5 — this
# assertion is why the artifact is re-cut. It lived at the tail of the path test,
